{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/108336-jade-mountain-versus-earth-dragon-style","id":108336,"title":"Jade Mountain versus Earth Dragon style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-08T10:46:49-07:00","id":108336,"title":"Jade Mountain versus Earth Dragon style","content":"In previous editions I always had seen Jade mountain style thematically as a terrestrial level version of the immaculate earth dragon style. In third edition both styles (should they exist) will presumably be able to be used at celestial level, terrestrial level and mortal level. So thematically having a terrestrial level earth dragon martial art is a function carried out by earth dragon style being practised at terrestrial level. <br /> <br /> If you were going to write up both martial arts, (I realize that dropping Jade mountain is a reasonable choice) how would you differentiate them? How would they feel or function differently from one another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:10:36-07:00","id":108362,"title":"","content":"Not speaking specifically to the current Charms of the two styles, because I expect those to change substantially, but rather to a thematic difference that could cross 'tiers': Earth Dragon should evoke t